<h2>Why a local factory matters</h2>
<p>Chandapura and the neighbouring Bommasandra and Jigani industrial areas are home to many of the workshops that make modular kitchens and wardrobes for South Bangalore. Living close to one is an advantage you should use.</p>
<?= img('factory-made-wardrobe-and-kitchen-modules', caption: 'Factory-made kitchen and wardrobe modules: machine-cut panels, pressed edge banding and pre-drilled hinge holes') ?>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Inspect before production.</strong> See the plywood or HDHMR sheets with their brand and grade stamps, and the laminate or acrylic sheets in daylight, before they are cut.</li>
  <li><strong>Check the machines.</strong> A panel saw, an edge-bander and a boring machine produce square, sealed, consistent panels. Hand-cut panels with glued edge tape do not last as long in the monsoon.</li>
  <li><strong>Shorter delivery and service.</strong> A loose hinge or a dropped drawer gets fixed in a day when the workshop is 3 km away, not in a week.</li>
  <li><strong>Fewer middlemen.</strong> A firm that designs and manufactures keeps the vendor's margin out of your quote and controls the delivery date.</li>
</ul>
<p>What to look for during a factory visit, and why machine-made modules last longer, is covered in <a href="/compare/modular-vs-carpenter-kitchen/">modular vs carpenter-made kitchens</a>.</p>

<h2>Independent houses and villas: what to plan</h2>
<h3>Several kitchens, one specification</h3>
<p>Houses with rental floors often need two to four kitchens. Fix one layout and one specification and repeat it: the factory cuts faster, you get a better rate, and repairs use the same parts. Keep the owner's kitchen in a better finish if you like, but use the same board and hardware brand throughout.</p>
<h3>Pooja room and staircase</h3>
<p>Ground-floor pooja rooms in houses here are often full rooms, not units. Plan the door, the storage for samagri and lamps and the ventilation together; see the <a href="/rooms/pooja-room/">pooja room guide</a> and <a href="/doors/pooja-room-door-design/">pooja room door designs</a>. Under-stair space suits a shoe and utility cabinet or a small study nook.</p>
<h3>Double-height living rooms</h3>
<p>Villas off Anekal and Dommasandra roads often have a double-height living room. Large walls need panelling, cladding or a tall bookshelf to feel finished, and lighting has to be planned at two levels. Ideas are in the <a href="/wall-design/">wall design guide</a> and the <a href="/planning/lighting-design/">lighting design guide</a>.</p>
<h3>Rental floors that last</h3>
<p>For floors you will let, durability and easy repair matter more than looks. Choose laminate shutters, BWP plywood under every sink, granite counters, hinged wardrobes with lofts and mainstream hardware. Skip gloss acrylic and sliding wardrobes, which show wear soonest.</p>

<h2>Local conditions to design for</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Hard water.</strong> Borewell and tanker water is common. Choose a steel 304 sink, seal granite after fixing, avoid glossy glass behind the sink and plan an RO point. The <a href="/modular-kitchen/electronic-city-chandapura/">local kitchen guide</a> has the full list.</li>
  <li><strong>Monsoon humidity.</strong> Store boards off the floor and indoors during June–October, seal every cut edge, and use BWP plywood near water.</li>
  <li><strong>Dust from roads and construction.</strong> Prefer closed storage, dust-sealing gaskets on wardrobe doors and handle-less grooves over open shelves.</li>
  <li><strong>Power cuts.</strong> Plan an inverter circuit for the fridge, the router and a few lights and fans before the false ceiling goes up.</li>
</ul>

